   "source": [
    "# Computer Vision Masterclass - Face detection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup and files\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook uses OpenCV Haar cascades and optional dlib detectors. Install the dependencies in your environment before running the code:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "pip install opencv-python\n",
    "pip install dlib  # optional; needed only for the HOG and CNN sections\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Put the sample files in a `data/` folder beside this notebook, using `Images/`, `Cascades/`, and `Weights/` subfolders. The image and cascade files used by these examples are not included. The dlib CNN section also requires `Weights/mmod_human_face_detector.dat`; without it, that section is skipped. If you use Google Colab, mount Drive and either copy the assets into `data/` or change `DATA_DIR` in the setup cell below.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the setup cell before the examples. Missing required images or Haar cascade files produce a descriptive error with the expected path.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "NgQKD4_BSOPP"
   },
   "source": [
    "## OpenCV"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "w8zOtNhKLp-Z"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Loading the image"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "oge5c1WGoOk_"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import cv2\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep all external project assets in one predictable location.\n",
    "DATA_DIR = Path(\"data\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_image(path):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Load a color image or raise a helpful error when it is absent/invalid.\"\"\"\n",
    "    path = Path(path)\n",
    "    image = cv2.imread(str(path))\n",
    "    if image is None:\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "            f\"Could not load image: {path.resolve()}\\n\"\n",
    "            \"Check that the file exists and is a supported image format.\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    return image\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_cascade(path):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Load an OpenCV cascade and report missing or invalid XML files clearly.\"\"\"\n",
    "    path = Path(path)\n",
    "    detector = cv2.CascadeClassifier(str(path))\n",
    "    if detector.empty():\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "            f\"Could not load Haar cascade: {path.resolve()}\\n\"\n",
    "            \"Check that the cascade XML file exists and is valid.\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    return detector\n"
   ]
  },
